BND-01: give a FREE/NORMAL outfall below a regulator no offset depth

setAllOutfallDepths() sets a FREE outfall to z + min(yNorm, yCrit) and a
NORMAL one to z + yNorm. For a weir, orifice or outlet whose downstream node
is the outfall, legacyOffset() returned the regulator's un-raised crest
(legacy offset2), which is a height above the UPSTREAM node, so the outfall
got the crest height as a fake tailwater depth. Return 0 for that case, as
the 5.3.0 patch does; conduits are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-01_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydraulics/Outfall.cpp b/src/engine/hydraulics/Outfall.cpp
index 3fd3a23..55ecf16 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydraulics/Outfall.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydraulics/Outfall.cpp
@@ -126,12 +126,12 @@ static double getYnorm(const XSectParams& xs, double beta, double q_max,
 // weir/outlet crest in its side table and the orifice offset in offset1;
 // a pump has none.
 static double legacyOffset(const SimulationContext& ctx, std::size_t uk, bool downstream) {
-    // A regulator's downstream offset is legacy's un-raised crest (the
-    // resolver's WARNING-10 pass keeps it in offset2 before raising offset1
-    // / the side-table crest to the downstream invert).
+    // A regulator's downstream offset (legacy offset2) is its crest height
+    // above its UPSTREAM node, not a height above the outfall: it gives a
+    // downstream outfall no depth (legacy link_setOutfallDepth).
     if (downstream && ctx.links.type[uk] != LinkType::CONDUIT &&
         ctx.links.type[uk] != LinkType::PUMP)
-        return ctx.links.offset2[uk];
+        return 0.0;
     switch (ctx.links.type[uk]) {
         case LinkType::CONDUIT:
             return downstream ? ctx.links.offset2[uk] : ctx.links.offset1[uk];
